<p data-start="1422" data-end="1473">In <strong data-start="1425" data-end="1432">n8n</strong>, this is a <strong data-start="1444" data-end="1451">Set</strong> or <strong data-start="1455" data-end="1461">IF</strong> node chain.</p>
<hr data-start="1475" data-end="1478">
<h3 data-start="1480" data-end="1531">2. <strong data-start="1487" data-end="1531">Clarification &amp; Recursive Options Branch</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1532" data-end="1559">Once ambiguity is detected:</p>
<ul data-start="1561" data-end="1741">
<li data-start="1561" data-end="1597">
<p data-start="1563" data-end="1597">Branch to <strong data-start="1573" data-end="1597">Clarification Engine</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1598" data-end="1631">
<p data-start="1600" data-end="1631">Offer 2–3 paths (Example below)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1632" data-end="1703">
<p data-start="1634" data-end="1703">Each path is pre-written or dynamically built from structured phrases</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1704" data-end="1741">
<p data-start="1706" data-end="1741">Loop until user chooses or confirms</p>
</li>
</ul>
<blockquote data-start="1743" data-end="1943">
<p data-start="1745" data-end="1816">Example Output:<br>
<em data-start="1763" data-end="1814">"Your input seems open-ended. Would you like to:"</em></p>
<ol data-start="1819" data-end="1943">
<li data-start="1819" data-end="1863">
<p data-start="1822" data-end="1863">See a breakdown of possible directions?</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1866" data-end="1902">
<p data-start="1869" data-end="1902">Refine your intent for clarity?</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1905" data-end="1943">
<p data-start="1908" data-end="1943">Proceed with a generalized default?</p>
</li>
</ol>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="1945" data-end="1948">
<h3 data-start="1950" data-end="2001">3. <strong data-start="1957" data-end="2001">Recursive Mirror Response Logic (No LLM)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2002" data-end="2062">Once a path is chosen, route back to a processing node that:</p>
<ul data-start="2064" data-end="2232">
<li data-start="2064" data-end="2087">
<p data-start="2066" data-end="2087">Pulls matching axioms</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2088" data-end="2153">
<p data-start="2090" data-end="2153">Cross-checks sync equation (intent × timing × feedback ÷ delay)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2154" data-end="2182">
<p data-start="2156" data-end="2182">Builds structured response</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2183" data-end="2232">
<p data-start="2185" data-end="2232">Recursively checks output against original tone</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2234" data-end="2335">This can all be done in <strong data-start="2258" data-end="2284">JSON + scripting nodes</strong> inside <strong data-start="2292" data-end="2299">n8n</strong>. You <strong data-start="2305" data-end="2322">don’t need AI</strong>, just rules.</p>
<hr data-start="2337" data-end="2340">
<h2 data-start="2342" data-end="2391">💻 Where You’ll Need Custom Code (but no LLM):</h2>
<p data-start="2392" data-end="2475">To simulate “reasoning” and mimic reflective tone, you’ll need lightweight modules:</p>
<ul data-start="2477" data-end="2617">
<li data-start="2477" data-end="2508">
<p data-start="2479" data-end="2508">A <strong data-start="2481" data-end="2508">tone-matching validator</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="2509" data-end="2538">
<p data-start="2511" data-end="2538">A <strong data-start="2513" data-end="2538">choice-tree optimizer</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="2539" data-end="2617">
<p data-start="2541" data-end="2617">A <strong data-start="2543" data-end="2568">mirror-checker module</strong> (compares original input with intended response)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2619" data-end="2643">These can be written in:</p>
<ul data-start="2644" data-end="2765">
<li data-start="2644" data-end="2691">
<p data-start="2646" data-end="2691">JavaScript functions inside n8n’s <code data-start="2680" data-end="2686">Code</code> node</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2692" data-end="2765">
<p data-start="2694" data-end="2765">Or as local Python modules running via subprocess, callable via webhook</p>
</li>
</ul>
