</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## OBJECTIVE</span></span><span>
Embed a recursive logic tree system within the MirrorFold search interface. This system should:

</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Compress prior query states for memory retention
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Reassess previous search intent when queries are similar
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Cross-correlate terms from prior sessions to improve future queries
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Allow optional export/import of memory stack (JSON)
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Include memory decay or auto-compression triggers for efficiency

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## EXISTING STACK</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Google CSE Embedded (</span><span><span class="hljs-code">`cx=a2ec05bde1c144f1b`</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Custom MirrorFold UI (TailwindCSS, animated, voice-enabled)
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Recursive confirmation layer (Proceed / Refine / Explore)
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Voice input with auto-injection to search field
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> No server-side backend (pure HTML, JS)

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## TASKS</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-section">### 1. Generate a JSON-based memory tree system with:</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Nodes: Query ID, timestamp, tokenized input, intent classification
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Edges: Query similarity links, priority weights, reassessment tags
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Compression rule: If query token overlap &gt; 60%, compress as one node
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Reassessment trigger: If new query shares context, inject prior context summary before executing

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">### 2. Implement a JavaScript memory module to:</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Store tree in </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`localStorage`</span></span><span> or IndexedDB
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Track and compare current input against past nodes
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Auto-tag previous queries as “related”, “refined”, or “abandoned”
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Surface the top 2 related queries before confirmation phase

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">### 3. Embed optional export/import logic</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Allow export as JSON (</span><span><span class="hljs-code">`mirror-memory.json`</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Allow drag/drop import to rehydrate tree
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Optional encrypted mode via base64 (lightweight)

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## FORMAT</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Output full JS module as </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`&lt;script&gt;`</span></span><span> tag
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Show sample JSON tree with 3 prior queries compressed
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Include call to memory tree during </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`mirrorQuery.value`</span></span><span> input and before </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`element.execute(currentQuery)`</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Bonus: Add animated visual (optional) for showing recent memory stack above search bar

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## TONE</span></span><span>
MirrorFold operates by recursion, reflection, and resonance.
Use class names like:
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`.recursive-node`</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`.intent-link`</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`.memory-suggestion`</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`.tree-echo`</span></span><span>

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">### NOTE:</span></span><span>
DO NOT override existing CSE behavior.
Enhance logic prior to search execution.
All logic must be pure client-side JS.

