<p data-start="1227" data-end="1255">Now you just need to ensure:</p>
<ul data-start="1256" data-end="1604">
<li data-start="1256" data-end="1361">
<p data-start="1258" data-end="1361">The search logic connects into <code data-start="1289" data-end="1297">App.js</code> and either writes to or pulls from the memory compression tree.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1362" data-end="1508">
<p data-start="1364" data-end="1508">If you're embedding the CSE script (from earlier), place that either in a <code data-start="1438" data-end="1458">SearchComponent.js</code> or as part of a <code data-start="1475" data-end="1486">useEffect</code> hook inside <code data-start="1499" data-end="1507">App.js</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1509" data-end="1604">
<p data-start="1511" data-end="1604">Optionally, wrap that query logic in <code data-start="1548" data-end="1559">try/catch</code> and set a state variable for query tracking.</p>
</li>
</ul>
