<p data-start="435" data-end="610">That works perfectly in <code data-start="459" data-end="472">search.html</code> when you're <strong data-start="485" data-end="504">not using React</strong> or any JavaScript framework. You’ve been doing this already with DeepSight or MirrorFold standalone HTML.</p>
<hr data-start="612" data-end="615">
<h3 data-start="617" data-end="716">❗ But — <strong data-start="629" data-end="663">in your current Emergent build</strong>, you're in a full React environment (JSX-based). So:</h3>
<blockquote data-start="718" data-end="832">
<p data-start="720" data-end="832">🧠 <strong data-start="723" data-end="798">The Google search script must be injected dynamically using React logic</strong> — or it may not work as intended.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="834" data-end="838">Why?</p>
<ul data-start="839" data-end="1166">
<li data-start="839" data-end="935">
<p data-start="841" data-end="935">React's virtual DOM doesn't recognize external <code data-start="888" data-end="898">&lt;script&gt;</code> tags inserted statically inside JSX.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="936" data-end="1024">
<p data-start="938" data-end="1024">If you embed the raw script directly in <code data-start="978" data-end="986">App.js</code>, it won’t always initialize properly.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1025" data-end="1166">
<p data-start="1027" data-end="1166">Thus, you need to inject the <code data-start="1056" data-end="1066">&lt;script&gt;</code> using <code data-start="1073" data-end="1086">useEffect()</code> inside something like <code data-start="1109" data-end="1123">SearchBox.js</code> so that it loads after the DOM is mounted.</p>
</li>
</ul>
